-- The hostile reading: evidence for the findings of NOTES.md §4. Each assertion here states the
-- SURPRISING answer the encoding gives, so it passes; a reader should find each one wrong in
-- spirit, or at least not what a policyholder would expect. A finding that only reading can show
-- is in NOTES.md alone, marked "reading only".

§ `Findings`

§§ `Fixtures`

`as made`    MEANS `the decree as made`
`as amended` MEANS `the decree as amended by Decree 220/2026`

GIVEN h  IS A `The harm to the person`
      xs IS A LIST OF `A vehicle that caused the harm`
GIVETH A `A person harmed in a road accident`
`a person with` h `harmed by` xs MEANS
    `A person harmed in a road accident` WITH
        `the accident happened on`          IS YMD 2026 8 3
        `the harm`                          IS h
        `the vehicles that caused the harm` IS xs

GIVEN a IS A `The insurer's answer on the person's harm`
GIVETH A `A vehicle that caused the harm`
`an insured vehicle whose insurer answers` a MEANS `an identified, insured vehicle, whose insurer answers` a

GIVEN p IS A `A point of Article 12(3)`
      h IS A `The harm to the person`
      n IS A NUMBER
      f IS A `What was later found of the accident`
GIVETH AN `An advance an insurer paid`
`an advance under` p `for` h `of` n `, later` f MEANS
    `An advance an insurer paid` WITH
        `the point under which it was paid`                IS p
        `the harm, as estimated when the advance was paid` IS h
        `the amount advanced`                              IS n
        `what was later found of the accident`             IS f

GIVEN charged IS A NUMBER
      ground  IS A `A ground stated for the premium charged`
      vol     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An offer to sell the compulsory motor insurance`
`an offer at` charged `on` ground `, voluntary cover cheaper by` vol MEANS
    `An offer to sell the compulsory motor insurance` WITH
        `the premium of Annex I for the vehicle and the term`      IS 437000
        `the premium the offer charges`                            IS charged
        `the ground stated for the premium charged`                IS ground
        `the discount offered on payment`                          IS 0
        `benefits offered with the compulsory cover`               IS EMPTY
        `a reduction in the price of voluntary cover sold with it` IS vol

