§§ `R4 — the injured person's own intent bars support only where the vehicle was identified and insured`

-- A person who deliberately steps in front of a vehicle and dies: no support if the vehicle was
-- insured; 45,000,000 if it was uninsured or never identified (fork V7). And an advance paid to
-- that person under point (b), the accident later found excluded for that intent, is repaid to
-- the insurer: the repayment paragraph has no exception.
